{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For she was the mother of all living.</b> Why did he call her חַוָּה (Chavah) now, after the sin? And further, he should have called her חַיָּה (Chayah)! And it appears that before the sin she was called חַיָּה (Chayah) on account of 'mother of all living,' and after the sin, since she brought death upon the generations, her name was changed from חַיָּה (Chayah) to חַוָּה (Chavah), for חַוָּה (Chavah) is derived from the Aramaic root חִוְיָא, which means serpent. And the verse comes to explain why he did not call her 'serpent' explicitly — because beforehand she was the mother of all living and was called חַיָּה (Chayah), therefore when he changed her name he did not need to change anything except the yod (י״ד) to a vav (ו״ו), so that a trace of the first name would remain in its place."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:56.089378908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}